# THE STONES STAND DIFFERENTLY (docs/HUSH.md H2): in a crags ring one stone an
# epoch (Hush.EPOCH world minutes) stands turned, and a stone only takes its
# stance while nobody is looking. Frame the ring, go out of sight of it while an
# epoch passes, come back to the same place: one stone is not as it was (01
# against 02 from above, 03 against 04 over the shoulder), and the log says
# which turned and what its redraw cost.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/hush-stones.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
place the_crags
coast calm
near hush_ring
wait 1.0
shot 01-the-ring
walk 1,0 5.0 run
wait 0.5
hour 11.5
wait 1.5
near hush_ring
wait 1.0
await stone_turned 3
shot 02-back-an-epoch-later
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
wait 0.8
shot 03-the-ring-over-the-shoulder with shoulder
mouse 1100,0 0.8
wait 0.5
hour 12
wait 1.5
mouse -1100,0 0.8
wait 1.0
shot 04-looked-back-an-epoch-later with shoulder
